<!--
  BlockML VS Code — documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.vscode.documentation.V1Scope
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:contrib="org.blockml.bml.vscode.contribution"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.vscode.documentation"
  xmlns:theme="org.blockml.bml.vscode.theme"
  xmlns:vtype="org.blockml.bml.vscode.type">

  <name>V1Scope</name>
  <type>doc:V1Scope</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to VS Code plugin V1 features</is>

  <documentation>
    V1 (milestone ReleaseMilestone::V1) — minimal usable BML editing support:

    1. Simple syntax highlighting — TextMate grammar for XML-like BML structure: tags, attributes,
       comments, strings, and basic ${ } / &lt;$ $&gt; expression markers. No semantic resolution.
       Structured GrammarPattern entries in BlockMlExtension are SSOT; syntaxes/bml.tmLanguage.json
       is a render artefact. Framework vs domain tag coloring comes from the active HighlightScheme
       (theme:FrameworkRoles): root, identity, container, and facet tags use distinct TextMate
       scope families; other tags keep entity.name.tag.bml. Edit the scheme, then re-render
       patterns + tmLanguage via LLM — do not invent framework tag lists only in JSON.
    2. BML file type — language id bml, alias BlockML / BML, extension .bml. Language-configuration
       (block comments, brackets, autoClosingPairs) lives on LanguageContribution; the JSON file
       is a render artefact. Declarative V1 needs no extension main / activationEvents.
       xmlLanguageParticipant=true so vscode-xml still validates against bml.xsd via
       xsi:schemaLocation (files are language bml, not xml).
    3. File icon — icon theme blockml-icons (icons/blockml-icon-theme.json) maps .bml / language
       bml to icons/blockml.svg for explorer, tabs, and language association.
    4. Marketplace icon — use icons/blockml.png as the large VS Code Marketplace / Open VSX gallery
       icon (package.json icon field on Extension). Distinct from the filetype SVG.

    5. Color theme — BlockML (theme:BlockMlDevColorTheme, ColorThemeContribution.marketplace=true)
       ships as a Marketplace Themes listing. Position-based *.bml TextMate scopes are not painted
       by generic Dark+/Light+ families, so this custom theme is required for visible syntax
       highlighting. package.json contributes.themes[].id is ColorTheme.themeId (blockml);
       workbench.colorTheme in .vscode/settings.json defaults to it during extension development.

    Out of scope for V1: language server, semantic tokens, cross-file navigation, and rich settings
    beyond the ConfigurationContribution already declared for forward-compatible V2 keys.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="doc:V2Scope" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — V2 language server, advanced highlighting, navigation.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:LanguageContribution" relation="Defines">
      File type / language id contribution.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:GrammarContribution" relation="Defines">
      Simple TextMate grammar contribution.
    </see>
    <see type="theme:FrameworkRoles" relation="Defines">
      Default semantic highlight scheme for framework tag roles.
    </see>
    <see type="theme:BlockMlDevColorTheme" relation="Defines">
      Shipped Marketplace color theme required for visible BML syntax highlighting.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:MarketplaceListing" relation="SeeAlso">
      Marketplace README.md listing copy (V1 limitation + V2 language server).
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:IconContribution" relation="Defines">
      BML file icon contribution.
    </see>
    <see file="icons/blockml.svg" relation="Requires">
      Filetype icon asset for .bml / language bml in VS Code.
    </see>
    <see file="icons/blockml.png" relation="Requires">
      Large Marketplace gallery icon (package.json icon).
    </see>
    <see type="vtype:ReleaseMilestone" relation="SeeAlso">
      V1 / V2 milestone enum.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
